# E550 — CMake 库的显式动态/静态构建开关映射
id: E550
trigger_tool: cmake|conan
phase: configuration|packaging|testing
error_signature: DISABLE_DYNAMIC|DISABLE_STATIC|CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE|no registered CTest tests
severity: 1
category: cmake-conan-build-mode-binding
match_keywords: CMake cache variable, DISABLE_DYNAMIC, DISABLE_STATIC, shared option, static library, fPIC, Conan, CMakeDeps
title: Bind Conan library mode to upstream CMake cache switches and an API consumer
root_cause: Some CMake libraries read project-specific cache variables for dynamic and static targets without declaring them as CMake options; leaving those variables at defaults can package an unintended target set, while a project with no CTest registration can pass without exercising its public API.
affected_scope: CMake-based C or C++ libraries that expose separate static/shared targets and do not register upstream CTest cases.
verification_cmd: Configure with shared=false and fPIC=true, inspect the CMake cache and installed library names, then build a CMakeDeps consumer that calls a public API and run it when the target is executable.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: explicit-cache-mode-and-consumer
rec_description: Map Conan shared/fPIC options to the upstream dynamic/static cache variables, set CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE for static builds, and require a consumer test that links the installed target and calls a real public API.
rec_command: cmake -S . -B build -DDISABLE_DYNAMIC=ON -DDISABLE_STATIC=OFF -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conanfile-generate-and-test-package
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: ctest-inventory-only
fallback_description: If the upstream project truly has no registered tests, freeze an explicit empty upstream inventory and use the consumer test as the package-level functional check.
fallback_command: ctest --test-dir build --show-only=json-v1 --no-tests=error
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manifest-and-consumer
forbid_1_pattern: omit.*DISABLE_DYNAMIC|omit.*DISABLE_STATIC|upstream_tests.*NOT_RUN|consumer.*print
forbid_1_reason: Default target selection can package both modes or an unintended mode, and a print-only test does not prove headers and libraries come from the package.
forbid_1_consequence: Consumers may link the wrong artifact or a system fallback while the build is reported successful.
principles: R26,R34
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
